### Design Rationale:

1. **"find red_stained_glass"** → `position_near_with_facing` (preferred rule for find/locate tasks)
   - Target `[6, 2, 5]` is the center of the 8-pane red stained glass cluster on the front wall (x=4-8, y=2-3, z=5)
   - `max_distance=16` — generous range; the glass is only ~5 blocks from spawn so this triggers easily when the player faces the structure
   - `facing_tolerance=60` — ensures the player is actually looking toward the glass, not just nearby facing away

2. **"find nether_bricks"** → `position_near_with_facing` (preferred rule for find/locate tasks)
   - Target `[6, 2, 8]` is the volumetric center of the nether brick structure (x=3-9, y=0-5, z=5-11)
   - Same distance/tolerance parameters — the structure is massive so any approach while facing it will trigger
   - Distinct from the red glass milestone because the target point is deeper into the structure (z=8 vs z=5), but both can trigger from the same general area since the player faces forward

3. **"mine torch"** → `inventory_has` (preferred rule for mine tasks — mined item ends up in inventory)
   - Item is `"torch"` (NOT `"wall_torch"`) — CommonSenseAgent confirmed wall torches drop as regular torch items
   - `min_count=1` — player starts with empty inventory, so any torch proves mining occurred
   - Four torches available (two at eye-level y=2, two at y=3), giving the agent multiple opportunities

### Why NOT other rule types:
- Did NOT use `position_inside_box` for find tasks — that only checks position, not facing direction
- Did NOT use `count_in_box_at_least` for find tasks — finding doesn't require placing blocks
- Did NOT use `mine_block` event counter — `inventory_has` is more reliable and is the preferred mapping for mine tasks
